    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_content_HiKLPd": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Is it appropriate to wear a temple on a shirt?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>I get this one a lot, and I thought about it before I drew the first one. These are architectural drawings of a building, not anything that happens inside it. No slogans, nothing that turns the temple into a punchline. If you'd put a framed temple photo in your living room, this is that same idea on cotton.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_DJ79XT": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Is Peculiar People affiliated with the Church?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>No. We are an independent company. Peculiar People is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_iCLqdM": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Where do people usually wear these?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Our goal with our clothing is for it to be seen. Which means it also needs to be your go-to comfort clothing.<br/><br/>It's made to be the first thing you grab when you want to be comfortable, and the first clothing you'll be prompted to wear.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_6Py6Ex": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "How do I wash it so the print lasts?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Our prints are made to last. To make sure they do, use no bleach and no fabric softener, which coats the fibers and dulls the print over time. Don't iron over the design. You can wash it before the first wear to get the loose surface dye off, but you don't have to.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_WdJtJy": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "It says unisex. How do I size it if I want a women's fit?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>It's a men's cut. If you normally wear a women's medium, order a small for a fitted look or a medium if you want it roomier. The size guide video shows a woman at 5'9\" in a small and a man at 6'4\" in a large.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_rBijbT": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Where does the artwork come from?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Original line art, made here, one temple at a time. Every drawing gets checked against verified references before we add it to our collection.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_KDgPP7": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Do you do group orders?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. Ward and stake temple trips, mission reunions, family reunions. Email support@peculiarpeopleco.com with the temple, the garment, and roughly how many people, and I'll get back to you with a price.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "collapsible_row_content_YxXEG3": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "What is the digital art file?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p>An SVG of the temple line art for $4.95. Same drawing that goes on the shirts. It's a vector, so it scales to any size without going soft at the edges, and it opens in Cricut, Illustrator, Figma, or anything else that reads vectors.<br/><br/>This file should not be shared and is not permitted for commercial use.</p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
